.TH TSCLIENT 1 "November 2026" "TSClient 3.5.0"
.SH NAME
tsclient \- GTK4 frontend for remote desktop clients
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tsclient
.RI [ OPTIONS ] " [FILE]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
TSClient configures and launches rdesktop, FreeRDP, VNC viewers, Xnest,
and the Citrix ICA client. Install the backend needed for your connection.
RDPv4 and RDPv5 use rdesktop; RDP (FreeRDP) searches for xfreerdp3,
then xfreerdp, on PATH.
.PP
Open TSClient .tsc profiles or Windows .rdp files in UTF-8 or UTF-16.
Save As writes JSON .tsc profiles. Legacy TSClient profiles remain readable.
.PP
Interactive connections leave the settings window open. Connect becomes
Cancel while the client runs. Cancel or Exit terminates the direct client
process; descendants created by that client are not managed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show command-line help.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the application version.
.TP
.BR \-x " FILE, " \-\-execute= FILE
Launch a saved profile directly, without the settings window.
.TP
.I FILE
Open one profile in the settings window.
.SH PASSWORDS
New profile saves omit passwords, including automatic last.tsc saves.
Remember password in keyring is optional and requires a desktop Secret Service.
Connect, Save As, or Exit stores an opted-in password for the exact protocol,
server, username, and domain. Uncheck Remember and save, connect, or exit to
remove the saved credential for the current connection.
.PP
Changing connection identity clears the password field and resets Remember.
Keyring failures are reported without falling back to plaintext storage.
Older plaintext passwords are removed from a profile when that file is
saved again. Other profiles and backups are not automatically rewritten.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.tsclient/default.tsc
Startup profile, used before last.tsc if present.
.TP
.I ~/.tsclient/last.tsc
Settings saved when connecting or exiting.
.TP
.I ~/.tsclient/mru.tsc
Recent successful connections.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GSK_RENDERER
Overrides the renderer. TSClient defaults to cairo when this variable is unset.
.SH NOTES
The Flatpak bundles rdesktop. Other backends must be installed inside its
sandbox; installing them on the host does not make them available there.
.SH AUTHORS
TSClient contributors are listed in AUTHORS.
